# The trial of pod-extract in podvm (T-057, T-141), at podvm main 20ea781
# (pod-extract.commit: podvm took v0.10.0 and pod-oci, after c89b769, its
# fix of the whiteout escape, T-1698). The patch applies alone, also at
# e99fc9b (a record commit after it).
# crates/podvm-extract keeps podvm's glue and re-exports the crate:
# paths(store, digest) (<store>/rootfs/<digest>/rootfs and .meta.jsonl),
# extract(store, manifest, digest, out) (the layers of the manifest as blob
# paths of the store, podvm_probe::settings() for $PODVM_STORE in the space
# message, the line of each layer written to `out` when the extraction ends),
# is_extracted, remove_extracted, and Error { Extract(Failure),
# Image(podvm_image::Error) }. apply, layer, remove, safety, sidecar,
# whiteout, Extracted, DONE_MARKER and EXTRACT_HEADROOM_BYTES are
# pod_extract's. 11 files leave podvm (drive/whiteouts.rs too: the crate
# holds podvm's tests of the whiteout escape), and tar, flate2, ruzstd,
# serde, serde_json and sha2 leave crates/podvm-extract/Cargo.toml. The
# citations of the moved files name pod-extract, also those of T-1698. Each
# podcrates tag moves to v0.11.0, with the tags of podvm-enter and
# podvm-windows.
# The patch also takes T-139 of podcrates (PodUtils/podvm#222), as the
# adoption map of crates/pod-enter/README.md says: crates/podvm/src/ladder.rs,
# lifecycle/userland.rs and lifecycle/script.rs read the payload with
# ladder::payload_head and give the head to memfd::eligible, has_shebang and
# script_refusal; the memfd rung stages the open file with
# podvm_enter::memfd::stage_file (a wrapper of pod_enter::memfd::stage_file
# with podvm's names), in chunks. podvm's 128 MiB refusal of a payload goes:
# pod-enter has no ladder::PAYLOAD_CEILING, and no step holds the whole file.
# podvm's entry T-1647 waits for this take.
# podvm's tests of the touched crates (podvm-complete writes through
# pod_extract::safety; podvm-enter, podvm-windows and podvm-supervise take
# the new tag) and the integration tests that extract, refuse or start a
# payload;
# podvm's own path-safety experiment against the binary (crafted layers in
# a hand-built store: four refusals, the legal symlinks, nothing outside);
# clippy of the workspace and rustfmt of the touched crates, as podvm's
# gate.yml runs them; the runtime-state rows; podvm's record gate; each Rust
# toolchain of the workflows against the rust-version of podcrates; and the
# binary `podvm` for x86_64 musl, with podcrates' static check.
# podvm's binary embeds its interposer objects (crates/podvm/build.rs), and
# the tests of qol need them on a host that denies chroot(2), as a runner
# does. podvm's gate.yml builds them before the binary; the trial does the
# same.
cargo build -q --release -p podvm-gate --bin podvm-interpose-build
mkdir -p target/release && cp "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/podvm-interpose-build" target/release/
./target/release/podvm-interpose-build
cargo test -q -p podvm-extract
cargo test -q -p podvm-complete
cargo test -q -p podvm-enter -p podvm-windows -p podvm-supervise
cargo test -q -p podvm --bin podvm
cargo test -q -p podvm --test store_gates
cargo test -q -p podvm --test qol
cargo test -q -p podvm --test detached_stdio
cargo test -q -p podvm --test curated_refusals
cargo clippy -q --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo fmt -p podvm-extract -p podvm-complete -p podvm-enter -p podvm -p podvm-gate -p podvm-release --check
cargo build -q -p podvm --bin podvm
PODVM="${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podvm" bash experiments/220-extract-path-safety.sh
# podvm's gate finds the root of the repository from the path of its binary,
# so it runs from target/release/, with document-state beside it (gate.yml).
cargo build -q --release -p podvm-gate && cargo build -q --release -p podvm-release --bin document-state
mkdir -p target/release && cp "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/podvm-gate" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/document-state" target/release/
# docs/runtime-state.md lists each direct git or registry dependency with its
# locked version. The patch gives the rows of the git form (pod-core,
# pod-enter, pod-extract, pod-guest, pod-hostprobe, pod-proxy, pod-supervise,
# pod-term and pod-tls at 0.11.0); the trial's path form has no row for them. Each other row of the
# patch must be the generated one.
grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md > target/runtime-state.patch.md && python3 scripts/document-state.py --write && grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md | diff target/runtime-state.patch.md -
# The experiment above wrote its reading; the gate checks the tree as the
# patch leaves it.
git checkout -- experiments/results/extract-path-safety.txt
./target/release/podvm-gate
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
sh "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-static.sh" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podvm"
